	(text "IM69D120 (Infineon datasheet rev 1.0, 2017-12-20): VDD 1.62-3.6 V; 3.072 MHz lies in the 2.9-3.3 MHz operating range\n  (no mode-entry restriction; start-up 20 ms), clock duty 48-52 % at >= 2.9 MHz, rise/fall 13 ns; IDD 980 uA typ;\n  -26 dBFS, SNR 69 dB(A); ambient <= 70 C above VDD 3.0 V. SELECT has no stated internal pull: driven by the SEL wire via R5.\nCable (JST SR 1.0, A05SR05SR30K305B, both ends cut, soldered to J1): 1 VDD, 2 GND, 3 CLK, 4 SEL, 5 DATA - SEL is static,\n  so it separates CLK from DATA like a ground. Default: U1 fitted, R4 33 Ohm, R5 0 Ohm.\nLevers (bench 2.5): U1 bypass = U1 removed, its pads 2-4 bridged with wire (R3 dropped for space); R4 100 Ohm.\nTest points: the wire pads (no TP1-TP4, decision 9.1).\nPassives 0603 (D42); ESD in SOD-523 (D42: leaded alternative to the X1SON); MK1 LGA (no leaded MEMS exists).\nDecision 8.1 (2026-11-07): SPH0641LU4H-1 dropped - it must not start in ultrasonic mode (3.072-4.8 MHz), where the XU316 runs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 160.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5a8f655b-9c6f-41f8-a908-d53e73c17dbd")
	)
